.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH tine-edit 1  "edit " 
.SH NAME
tine\-edit \- Replace a block\*(Aqs text, as typing it into the block would: hidden properties (id::, collapsed::) and children are kept
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtine edit\fR [\fB\-g\fR|\fB\-\-graph\fR] [\fB\-\-debug\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-rev\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIBLOCK\fR> <\fITEXT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Replace a block\*(Aqs text, as typing it into the block would: hidden properties (id::, collapsed::) and children are kept
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-g\fR, \fB\-\-graph\fR \fI<GRAPH>\fR
The graph. Defaults to $TINE_GRAPH, else the graph folder around the current directory
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR
Enable diagnostic logging for the desktop app
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the typed result (schema tine.cli/1) as JSON
.TP
\fB\-\-rev\fR \fI<REV>\fR
Write only if the page is still at this rev (as `page show` prints it); required for a bare PAGE/POS without a fingerprint
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIBLOCK\fR>
The block: its id:: UUID, or PAGE/POS~FP as a read prints it
.TP
<\fITEXT\fR>
The new text; `\-` reads it from standard input
